REMEDIATION

Vulnerability:
vsFTPd 2.3.4 Backdoor

CVE:
CVE-2011-2523

Affected Service:
FTP (21/tcp)

Finding:

The assessment confirmed that the target was running vsFTPd 2.3.4 and was vulnerable to the known backdoor vulnerability. Exploitation resulted in a root-level command shell on the laboratory target.

Recommended Remediation:

1. Remove the vulnerable version of vsFTPd.

2. Upgrade the FTP service to a secure and supported version.

3. If FTP is not required, disable and remove the service completely.

4. Restrict access to FTP services using firewall rules and network segmentation.

5. Avoid exposing unnecessary services to untrusted networks.

6. Regularly scan systems for outdated software and known vulnerabilities.

7. Monitor authentication and network activity for suspicious connections.

ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS:

All testing documented in this project was performed against an intentionally vulnerable laboratory machine that I own or have explicit permission to test.

The activities were conducted for educational and authorized security testing purposes only.
